00:18:49.220 --> 00:19:01.920
And then this is, we haven't really talked about this part yet, but in the dinosaur segments, you will fight like a boss boss, and then they will drop a key for a door that is right in front of you.

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:10.520
Um, that, you know, in any other sense, you could have just had it be, you beat the boss, and then you move forward to the next level.

00:19:10.820 --> 00:19:15.080
There's no reason to pick up a key and then walk to a door that is a couple steps away.

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.800
So that must mean something to them too.

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:20.140
Like, what does all of this mean?

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:22.740
Did you get that?

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:26.200
Like, what, why, like, how pointless some of these things that you do are?

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:34.640
Yeah, like, I, I guess, you know, what you just mentioned about the key wouldn't be an issue, but it does feel like what Mike said, the, the Newgrounds thing.

00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:37.000
It's like, they had these ideas, but they just didn't really implement them.

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:44.560
And like, I was just gonna say that, that, that Newgrounds statement is like a statement that I have searched for so many times on this podcast.

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:48.820
Like, I've had that exact feeling, but didn't really remember the site I was thinking of.

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:50.320
It's a template for a game.

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:56.180
Yeah, like that is, there's been, we've had so many games that have felt like that, and that's like a, that's like a great description of like what this feels.

00:19:56.200 --> 00:20:01.320
Like, it's like, yeah, they have all the elements and they put them together in a way that you can technically play the game.

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:17.400
Well, before you become or jump into your cyberosaurus, there is an amazing, uh, non-animated cutscene of the cybersaurus that is very detailed and has some amazing sprite work.

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:30.500
But before you even jump into it and have the, uh, the nice little, uh, detailed sprite there, there's like a size, uh, that you can appreciate of the cybersaurus next to Professor Proteus.

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:38.360
When you get back to the beginning of the level after traversing through the empty parts, you see your cybersaurus there and it's significantly bigger than Professor Proteus.

00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:49.440
We're like seeing just a portion of the head and then we are greeted with this awesome cutscene, uh, and I keep saying cutscene, but it's really just still pixel art of the cybersaurus.

00:20:49.740 --> 00:20:51.660
But it's like nicely shadowed and everything.

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:53.120
Like, I really appreciate it.

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:54.700
Yeah, it paints a good picture.

00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:58.180
Then you play as cybersaurus and you're, what a disappointment.

00:20:58.180 --> 00:21:04.200
You're exactly, you're going from this huge mech to exactly the same size as Professor Proteus in his parts of the stages.

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:10.860
So everything is just shrunken down in scale again to the other dino bots where like they, it's fine.

