00:25:52.460 --> 00:26:02.980
The fact that you're this giant mech, mech Godzilla sort of thing, and yet you're still the size of a normal sprite from a side scroller.

00:26:02.980 --> 00:26:22.220
Um, it kind of removes a lot of the, uh, the potential for spectacle, um, that you can do with, I mean, and I'm not saying that that's an excuse because there, there are plenty of games that use this like sort of default height that still look great and, and give you a feeling of power.

00:26:22.220 --> 00:26:27.880
But if that's the whole idea is scale, this is not really the way you're going to do it.

00:26:28.100 --> 00:26:39.740
Like, and, and so the, the, the powers that you get, if they're still trying to give him some kind of feeling of scale, they're going to give him the sort of sludgy movement that he has.

00:26:40.060 --> 00:26:41.920
You're going to have to have better power ups.

00:26:42.020 --> 00:26:43.020
And they just didn't do that.

00:26:43.500 --> 00:26:52.100
And, and to be, to be honest to me, when I played this, what it felt like was when you play as whatever his name is, professor, whatever.

